Z||000004||firstfiero||04-13-2001||10:40 AM||||    yep...when I test drove my car the tank was on empty so my friend who i bought it from threw me the keys and some cash and said put some gas in her. Well after spending 10 min at the gas station looking like a complete idiot...I finnaly called him on my cell phone. He still makes fun of me. lol<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||14
Z||000005||rogergarrison||04-13-2001||12:59 PM||||me too. I didnt think Id ever find the release, they shoulda marked it on dash or something. On 50's cars they made a game out of hiding the actual filler cap. 57 chevy a piece of fin moulding was hinged, 56 chevy the taillite was acctually hinged with the cap behind it. Lots had a chrome door that fit flush with bumper face. VW had to open the front trunk to find filler. On a real Ferrari 308/328 the filler is behind the louver/fake hinged window behind driver-even has a rubber flap so u dont splash your fender.||||reg||1
